{"node":{"id":"MONDO:0012794","label":"ANE syndrome","definition":"ANE syndrome is a rare, genetic, neuro-endocrino-cutaneous disorder characterized by highly variable degrees of alopecia, moderate to severe intellectual disability, progressive, late-onset motor deterioration and combined anterior pituitary hormone deficiency, manifesting with central hypogonadotropic hypogonadism, delayed or absent puberty, growth hormone deficiency (resulting in short stature), progressive central adrenal insufficiency and a hypoplastic anterior pituitary gland. Additional features include hypodontia, flexural reticulate hyperpigmentation, gynecomastia, microcephaly and kyphoscoliosis.","synonyms":["alopecia, neurologic defects, and endocrinopathy syndrome","alopecia-progressive neurological defect-endocrinopathy syndrome","anes"],"xrefs":["DOID:0112244","GARD:0016987","MEDGEN:394313","MESH:C567425","OMIM:612079","Orphanet:157954","UMLS:C2677535"],"parents":[],"parents_labels":{},"children":[],"children_labels":{},"in_core":false,"cluster_id":null,"is_group":false,"n_genes":1,"n_phenotypes":36,"mechanism_classes":[]},"genes":[{"id":"e_99723316126c","source":"MONDO:0012794","target":"RBM28","type":"caused_by","evidence":[{"db":"Orphanet","origin":"Orphanet","record":"ORPHA:157954","level":"curated","date":"2026-06-23","url":"https://www.orpha.net/en/disease/detail/157954","confidence":0.95,"snippet":"Disease-causing germline mutation(s) (loss of function) in (Assessed) — RNA binding motif protein 28"},{"db":"HPO","origin":"OMIM","record":"OMIM:612079","level":"curated","date":"2026-09-02","confidence":0.9,"url":"https://omim.org/entry/612079","snippet":"RBM28 is annotated as disease gene of OMIM:612079 (HPO genes_to_phenotype, OMIM-derived)"}],"contradicting":[],"confidence":0.95,"independent_sources":["OMIM","Orphanet"],"level":"curated"}],"phenotypes":[{"edge":{"id":"e_15d6d8a472f5","source":"MONDO:0012794","target":"HP:0002333","type":"has_phenotype","evidence":[{"db":"HPO","ori